From: mrdidit <26687854+mrdidit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd-mbhc: drain jack work before releasing state

Cancel plug-detection work outside its mutex to avoid deadlocking a
worker waiting for that lock. Drain correction work after its producer
and delayed button work before freeing MBHC state. This is required
for safe consumer teardown when the measurement supplier is removed.

---

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c
@@ -1650,10 +1650,12 @@
 	free_irq(mbhc->intr_ids->mbhc_btn_press_intr, mbhc);
 	free_irq(mbhc->intr_ids->mbhc_sw_intr, mbhc);
 
+	/* Plug detection can queue correction work. */
+	cancel_work_sync(&mbhc->mbhc_plug_detect_work);
 	mutex_lock(&mbhc->lock);
 	wcd_cancel_hs_detect_plug(mbhc,	&mbhc->correct_plug_swch);
-	cancel_work_sync(&mbhc->mbhc_plug_detect_work);
 	mutex_unlock(&mbhc->lock);
+	wcd_cancel_btn_work(mbhc);
 
 	kfree(mbhc);
 }
